[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
NVIDIA CUDA rendering in Cycles (CYCLES_CUDA option)

FreeBSD's nvidia-driver has no native CUDA library, so the blender wrapper
loads the Linux one through nv-sglrun (emulators/libc6-shim).  This needs
the Linux NVIDIA libraries of exactly the same version as the loaded kernel
module (see `sysctl hw.nvidia.version`):

  GeForce GTX 9xx/10xx (Maxwell, Pascal) and Volta:
    x11/nvidia-driver-580 + x11/linux-nvidia-libs-580
  Newer GPUs:
    x11/nvidia-driver + x11/linux-nvidia-libs

The linux-nvidia-libs packages conflict with each other, remove the one that
does not match first.  libc6-shim also needs the Linux compatibility layer:

  sysrc linux_enable=YES && service linux start

Then select the GPU in Edit > Preferences > System > Cycles Render Devices
> CUDA.  OptiX is not available on FreeBSD.

Set BLENDER_NO_NV_SGLRUN=1 to start blender without nv-sglrun.  If no GPU is
listed, start it from a terminal to see why:

  BLENDER_NV_DEBUG=1 blender --debug-cycles --log-level info
EOM
}
]
